{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Declaring-a-macro","title":"Declaring a macro","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their own."}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes its kind as an argument. A client that registers one kind of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thing (routes, events, migrations) gives it a macro that fixes the kind instead, so its users"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":" and never see a number. That takes three declarations."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The client’s compiler plugin, a "},{"code":".macro","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" target that depends on this module, names the kind:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The client’s library declares the macro and the same kind for reading. It re-exports LinkerSets,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because the expansion names LinkerSets’ types in its users’ files:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    public static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Route() = #externalMacro(module: \"RoutesMacros\", type: \"RouteMacro\")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its users then register and find routes:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["enum Endpoints {","    @Route static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","}","","let endpoints = LinkerSet<Endpoint>(kind: .routes).values"]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"},{"type":"text","text":" writes the same record "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" writes, in the same section, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diagnostics name the client’s attribute ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'@Route' applies to static members only"},{"type":"text","text":"). Each kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a set of its own, so two clients in one program never see each other’s records as long as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their kinds differ. Kind 0 is reserved, and the expansion refuses it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro that takes its kind as an argument can return ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"LinkerSetsMacroSupp